Wizards start with force bolt spell.  When I first started playing
wizards I wondered if that meant "force the bolt on the door to break
the lock" or "a bolt of force".  Whichever it means when you break down
a door with a spell of force bolt it counts as a successful cast and
counts towards enhancing the combat spell school.  Once I figured that
out I ended my explorations of each level early on by going around
closing and blasting all non-shop and non-shrine doors on each level
until I am offered to enhance that spell skill.

When I read through the code I concluded that kicking down doors helps
build skill at kicking.  If I understand that correctly it contributes
to martial arts skill but not to bare handed combat skill.  So to me
playing a class that has martial arts it makes sense to end my
explorations of each level early on by closing and kicking down all
non-shop and non-shrine doors on each level until I am offered to
enhance my martial arts skill.

That doesn't cover all classes but it does suggest that kicking down
doors should not automatically be considered a bad idea.  A bad idea
before exploring and clearing out the rest of the level, sure.  Once
explored and cleared it depends.

